at actually seems to be the case  expect a challenge when facing max level  amiibo figures and should you change  tactics the amiibo really does respond  perhaps by baiting you to attack or by  spamming ranged attacks to try and  create an opening if you don't have  friends around and ever get sick of the  single-player options  amiibos are great additions even if they  are a little pricey for most players the  goal of all this training is to test  your skills against friends and that's  where smash brothers for Wii U really  excels turning item drops up to high in  cramming eight players into a relatively  small space is a very special kind of  unbridled lunacy  you can still play standard matches with  four combatants and that's as great as  it's always been there are quite a few  new stages in which to slug it out and  more than enough to provide a good  variety many levels change dramatically  over time and force you to keep up with  the shift and as long as you're not  looking for serious competition it's  always hilarious to watch unwitting  folks fall because they weren't  expecting the bottom of the level to  suddenly drop away and if the great  diversity of stages isn't enough for you  you can use the Wii U gamepad to create  your own levels there are too many  restrictions on size and there aren't a  lot of tools available but drawing  ridiculous levels with a touch pad more  than makes up for it sadly you can't  have eight player matches on custom  stages online multiplayer is the game's  bigger problem the five-second countdown  that marks the conclusion  timed match could take more than a  minute where the entire match may be so  laggy is to be unplayable online play is  extremely hit or miss and while the hits  are sublime  the misses are absolutely maddening  thankfully local play is absolutely  incredible  between the masterpiece collections  which are short demos of the classic  games that inspired Smash Brothers many  fighters and stages and the deep  character customization for fine-tuning  your fighters to suit your play style to  extensive screen shot editing tools  there's just so much to do with the Wii  U release Smash Brothers has fully  realized its goals there's something  here for nearly everyone from young to  old casual the hardcore presented almost  without compromise the game invites  everyone to join its undiluted joyous  celebration of the broad community that  Nintendo has built over the past 40  years  you
 

